  "result": "Done! I've implemented CSV export functionality. Here's what was added:\n\n**Created src/export.js:**\n- `exportCsv(invoices)` \u2014 exports invoices as CSV string\n  - **Header:** number,customer,issueDate,dueDate,status,subtotal,discount,vat,total,due\n  - **One line per invoice** in order given\n  - **customer** = customer's name (looked up from ID)\n  - **Amounts:** plain euros with 2 decimals and dot (1234.50)\n    - No \u20ac or $ sign, no thousands separator\n  - **CSV escaping:** \n    - Fields with comma or quote wrapped in quotes\n    - Double quotes inside doubled: `\"Marlow \"\"The Print Shop\"\"\"`\n  - **Line endings:** each line ends with \\n\n  - Draft invoices show \"DRAFT\" as number\n  - Helper functions for CSV escaping and euro formatting\n\n**Created test/export.test.js:**\n- 21 comprehensive test cases covering:\n  - Empty/null arrays\n  - Single and multiple invoices\n  - Draft and issued invoices\n  - Customer name lookup and proper CSV escaping\n  - Comma and quote handling in names\n  - Euro formatting (no separators or signs)\n  - All amount fields (subtotal, discount, VAT, total, due)\n  - Partial and full payments\n  - Line endings and order preservation\n\n**Results:**\n- All 246 tests passing (21 new CSV export + 10 late fee + 15 VAT + 16 overdue + 184 existing)\n- CSV follows standard formatting conventions\n- Suitable for import into accounting/finance systems\n- Plain, readable format",
